From 058a7def226fda58f9f0bf29f1411995e5c5ffe0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rocm-ernic CI <ci@rocm-ernic.invalid>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 12:05:07 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] ionic: stop on a failed SRQ receive prepare

ionic_post_recv_srq() ran both preparation helpers for their side effects
and then carried on regardless of what they returned.

ionic_v1_prep_recv()'s result was stored in rc but not acted on, and
ionic_v1_prep_defer_recv()'s was discarded entirely -- it is declared int
and returns -signed_len from ionic_v1_prep_pld() when a scatter-gather
list will not fit. Either way the loop fell through to the same two
statements:

	srq->in_use++;
	wr = wr->next;

so a work request that was never prepared was counted as occupying a slot,
the walk moved past it, and the next iteration overwrote rc -- with
success, if that one worked. Three things go wrong from one missing check.
in_use drifts up until it reaches queue.mask and the queue reports itself
permanently full; *bad points at the work request after the one that
failed, so a caller that retries from *bad silently drops the bad one; and
the caller is told the whole list posted.

Break on a non-zero rc, before the accounting. The out: path is unchanged
and still rings the doorbell for whatever was prepared before the failure,
which is what a partial post should do.
---
 providers/ionic/ionic_verbs.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/providers/ionic/ionic_verbs.c b/providers/ionic/ionic_verbs.c
index 7e1b06bf..30931a5d 100644
--- a/providers/ionic/ionic_verbs.c
+++ b/providers/ionic/ionic_verbs.c
@@ -3574,11 +3574,14 @@ static int ionic_post_recv_srq(struct ibv_srq *ibsrq, struct ibv_recv_wr *wr,
 			}
 
 			/* Prepare wqe and push it to pending list */
-			ionic_v1_prep_defer_recv(srq, ctx, wr);
+			rc = ionic_v1_prep_defer_recv(srq, ctx, wr);
 		} else {
 			rc = ionic_v1_prep_recv(&srq->rq, ctx, wr);
 		}
 
+		if (rc)
+			break;
+
 		srq->in_use++;
 		wr = wr->next;
 	}
